From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kitsune <km2077@foxmail.com>
Date: Fri, 26 Dec 2025 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: filogic: update GL.iNet GL-MT5000 support

Port of the review-feedback changes accumulated on PR openwrt#24237,
as incorporated by dmsza/openwrt branch openwrt-main-mt5000
(commit 8461b1b79b), review feedback from @dmtpascoal and @openwrt-ai:

- rtl8366ub: VLAN 1 default entry no longer carries all member/untag
  ports (member = 0, untag = 0): no data VLAN reachable through the
  default PVID; the bridge default_pvid 1 gets programmed per port.
- rtl8366ub: enforce accept-tagged-only on the CPU port at setup so a
  stray untagged conduit frame is never classified by the CPU PVID
  (cf. sja1105 drop_untagged on CPU/DSA ports).
- rtl8366ub-8021q tagger: move DSA_TAG_PROTO_RTL8366UB_8021Q_VALUE
  from 32 to 200 (out-of-tree tagger; upstream v7.0 already uses
  30-32 and master is at 35 - avoids enum id collision).
- mtk_eth_soc NAPI patch: call mtk_unreg_dev() on the err_free_dummy
  path (error handling fix).
- DTS: rename mt7987a-gl-mt5000.dts -> mt7987a-glinet-gl-mt5000.dts
  (matches the glinet_* DEVICE naming convention), add serial0 alias
  and stdout-path, fix LED node names (led@N -> led-N), drop
  redundant SUPPORTED_DEVICES.
- filogic config: explicitly enable CONFIG_NET_DSA_TAG_RTL8366UB_8021Q.
- generic config: add "# ... is not set" defaults for other targets.

IMPORTANT - embedded hunk line counts are updated together with the
content changes above (rtl8366ub_dsa.c 993->1002, rtl8366ub_switch.c
430->433, plus the 795-11/795-12 count corrections from upstream
review). patch(1) honours the declared @@ counts, so inserting lines
without bumping them silently truncates the generated C files, which
broke the kernel build ("expected declaration or statement at end of
input" in rtl8366ub_switch.c).

Whitespace/checkpatch reformatting of the rtl8366ub driver from the
upstream update is intentionally NOT carried over; only the functional
changes are ported.

